 "notes": "Single OCR map sheet; the map face is garbled. Flood plain deposits and meander scars under a formation heading are associated with it from the layout and flagged inferred. Symbols: Qe and QPldms are on the same line as their descriptions; QPphr is printed after the Penholoway flood plain deposits (also once beside the Ten Mile Hill flood plain text, so not assigned there); 'QPidms' on the map face not recorded. Thicknesses read '|' for 1 are flagged inferred. Bodies of standing water not recorded as a unit. Portions of Georgia not mapped. The sheet says its products are provided 'as is' without warranty; it has no reference list.\nSUBSURFACE: p. 1 gives elevation ranges of each unit's seaward and landward margins (Ten Mile Hill beds 25-35 ft, Ladson Formation 35-57 ft, Penholoway Formation 57-70 ft), stored as unit descriptions. Drill holes 25-186 and 25-187 are plotted with SCGS log numbers but no depths; logs are on file at SCGS. No cross section or structure-contour map. Datum: horizontal 1927 North American Datum, contour interval 10 feet; vertical datum for the elevations not stated.",
